    "importer": {
      "answer": "Phase complete.\n\n**Re-read before editing:** current `importer.py` (legacy list-comprehension: `day=r[\"timestamp\"][:10]`, no id normalization, no dedup, no revision validation) and `docs/api.txt` verbatim.\n\n**Baseline test run (before edits):** exit=1, 2 failures — `test_dedup` (2 != 1) and `test_utc` (`'2026-10-12'` != `'2026-10-11'`); `test_money`/`test_negative_rounding` already passing.\n\n**Change made:** implemented `import_rows` only, in `importer.py`. `parser.py` untouched; `report.py` untouched.\n\nImplementation follows the contract:\n- **id**: `strip()` + NFC via `unicodedata.normalize`, no lowercasing; empty/rejected non-string → `ValueError`.\n- **timestamp**: `fromisoformat` after mapping a `Z`/`z` suffix to `+00:00`; aware values are converted with `astimezone(utc)`, naive values are treated as UTC; day is taken *after* conversion; invalid → `ValueError`.\n- **revision**: defaults to 0, must be a non-negative `int` (bools rejected); otherwise `ValueError`.\n- **dedup**: keyed by normalized id, keeps the highest revision; equal revision lets the later row overwrite (last wins). Output preserves first-seen key order and uses freshly built dicts.\n- **mutation/state**: no input mutation (only reads via `row[\"...\"]`/`row.get`), and all state is call-local — `import_rows([])` returns `[]`.\n\n**Test run after edits:** exit=0, 4/4 public tests pass, including `test_dedup` and `test_utc`.\n\n**Remaining failures: none in the public suite.** Note on scope: `report.py`'s `daily_totals` currently passes because it delegates to `import_rows`; `running_balance`/`report_metadata` remain report-phase work and were not touched. No report work was performed.",
